tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-135-l6-int-in-an-extern-group.hero:25:21: error[reserved_word]: `int` is not a word in this language — in an `extern` group a type is the header's own width and sign: `i32` where the header says `int`, `i64` where it says `int64_t`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-135-l6-int-in-an-extern-group.hero:25:29: error[reserved_word]: `int` is not a word in this language — in an `extern` group a result or a constant may be wider than the header's type: `i64` holds every C integer but an unsigned 64-bit one, which is `u64`
